                "schemeImageUrl": "",
                "briefDescription": "The scheme aims to encourage cardamom growers to adopt Improved Cardamom Curing Devices (ICCD) for drying small cardamom, thereby improving the quality of the produce and making it more suitable for export.",
                "detailedDescription_md": "The Integrated Scheme for Export Promotion &amp; Quality Improvement in Spices and Research &amp; Development of Cardamom: Post-Harvest Improvement – Improved Cardamom Curing Devices (ICCD) for Small Cardamom (Nos.) is implemented by the Spices Board India under the Ministry of Commerce and Industry, Government of India. The scheme aims to encourage cardamom growers to adopt Improved Cardamom Curing Devices (ICCD) for drying small cardamom, thereby improving the quality of the produce and making it more suitable for export. It is being implemented in accordance with the modalities and guidelines approved by the Competent Authority under the Integrated Scheme for Export Promotion &amp; Quality Improvement in Spices and Research &amp; Development of Cardamom during the 15th Finance Commission period (2021–22 to 2025–26).\n<br>\n\n",
                "benefits_md": "\n- 33.33 % of cost of unit, subject to a maximum of ₹ 1,50,000/- per unit for General Category and 75% subject to maximum of ₹ 3,37,500, per unit for SC/ST &amp; 90% Spice Producer&#39;s Groups in Identified Clusters subject to maximum of ₹ 4,00,000/-\n- Registered cardamom growers having a land holding size of 0.40 ha to 8 ha Assistance for groups/FPOs will be as in QGBG\n\n<br>\n\n",
                "exclusions_md": "<br>\n\n",
                "detailedDescription": [
                    {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "children": [
                            {
                                "text": "The Integrated Scheme for Export Promotion & Quality Improvement in Spices and Research & Development of Cardamom: Post-Harvest Improvement – Improved Cardamom Curing Devices (ICCD) for Small Cardamom (Nos.) is implemented by the Spices Board India under the Ministry of Commerce and Industry, Government of India. The scheme aims to encourage cardamom growers to adopt Improved Cardamom Curing Devices (ICCD) for drying small cardamom, thereby improving the quality of the produce and making it more suitable for export. It is being implemented in accordance with the modalities and guidelines approved by the Competent Authority under the Integrated Scheme for Export Promotion & Quality Improvement in Spices and Research & Development of Cardamom during the 15th Finance Commission period (2021–22 to 2025–26)."
                            }
                        ]
